    synopsis: "A paper artist's moon lantern escapes into the night and leads her to a neighbor who needs a little light.",
    chapterTitle: "The Moon That Floated Away",
    content: [
      "Every year, Bea folded paper moons for the town festival. This time, she made one from her grandfather's old map and tied it to a lantern. A gust lifted it from her hands and carried it over the rooftops. Bea followed its pale glow through quiet streets and into the garden of a house she had never visited.",
      "There she found Mr. Solis, an elderly neighbor who had been sitting alone in the dark since his porch light broke. The lantern had caught in his fig tree. Bea climbed the fence to retrieve it, but the branch bent and the paper moon began to tear. Mr. Solis steadied the ladder while she carefully freed it.",
      "They repaired the moon together with pieces of the map and walked to the festival side by side. Mr. Solis brought his old accordion, and Bea brought the lantern. It floated above the crowd, patched and shining. The best part of the festival, Bea realized, was not making something perfect; it was finding someone to share it with."
    ]
