      "Inside the tower, she found a retired clockmaker trying to restart the gears alone. The parcel held the missing brass key, but the stairwell was blocked by a fallen beam. Tess climbed the narrow outside ladder as wind shook the tower. With one careful reach, she passed the key through the broken window.",
      "The clock began to move again, striking midnight over the rooftops. The clockmaker revealed that he had sent the parcel years ago and forgotten where it was meant to go. Tess laughed and helped him finish the repair. The city woke to the sound of time returning, and the courier finally delivered the parcel to the person who needed it."
