      "At crane nine hundred, Keiko's hands cramped and she began to wonder if the promise mattered. Yumi sent a note saying she missed the school garden and wanted to see everyone again. Keiko brought the unfinished cranes to class, and her friends helped fold the rest, each adding a message of encouragement.",
      "They carried a thousand cranes to the hospital together. Yumi laughed at the uneven wings and chose her favorite. Recovery took time, but the cranes reminded her that she was not waiting alone. Keiko kept folding after the promise was done, because hope had become something they could make together."
