    synopsis: "A young apprentice repairs a clock that has stopped at the minute its maker promised to return.",
    chapterTitle: "The Stopped Minute",
    content: [
      "In the old clock shop, every clock worked except the one above the door. It had stopped at 4:17, the minute the clockmaker promised his daughter he would return from a journey. Years later, apprentice Lio found a note hidden inside the wooden case: 'The clock will move when the promise is kept.'",
      "Lio discovered the clockmaker had written letters to his daughter but never sent them, ashamed that he had been away so long. The daughter now lived across town and had never known he was still alive. Lio carried the letters through a snowstorm, but the bridge was closing for repairs.",
      "He crossed with the bridge crew just before sunset and delivered the letters. The daughter came to the shop the next morning. She forgave her father slowly, one conversation at a time. At 4:17, the clock began ticking again—not because the past was fixed, but because they had finally started keeping a new promise."
    ]
