  {
    id: 30, title: "Tomorrow's Notebook", author: "Samira Cole", genre: "Mystery", icon: "📓",
    synopsis: "A student finds a notebook filled with tomorrow's clues and uses its final page to prevent a preventable accident.",
    chapterTitle: "The Page Dated Tomorrow",
    content: [
      "On her desk, Nessa found a notebook dated tomorrow. Its first page described a red umbrella left on the library steps. The next morning, the umbrella was exactly where the note said. The book's later pages listed small events around school, all written in handwriting that looked like hers.",
      "The final page warned that a loose railing would give way during the afternoon assembly. Nessa told the principal, but no one believed a notebook. She tried to fix it alone and nearly fell. Instead, she found the custodian and showed him the loose bolts before the crowd arrived.",
      "The railing was repaired in time, and no one was hurt. The notebook's last page turned blank. Nessa never learned who had written it, but she began writing down the things she could change herself. Tomorrow did not need to be a mystery if someone paid attention today."
    ]
  }
